INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{}, 3, :assistant, "f4ccd4bb-d017-48da-bdbb-1171cb21bc88", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "  def total(quantity, unit_cents, discount_pct \\\\ 0)\n      when is_integer(quantity) and quantity >= 0\n      when is_integer(unit_cents) and unit_cents >= 0\n      when is_integer(discount_pct) and discount_pct >= 0 and discount_pct <= 100 do\n    gross = quantity * unit_cents\n    discounted = gross - div(gross * discount_pct, 100)\n    if quantity == 0 do\n      0\n    else\n      discounted + shipping_cents()\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp shipping_cents, do: 499", "old_string" => "  def total(quantity, unit_cents, discount_pct \\\\ 0) when quantity >= 0 do\n    gross = quantity * unit_cents\n    discounted = gross - div(gross * discount_pct, 100)\n    max(discounted - shipping_cents(), 0) + shipping_cents()\n  end\n\n  defp shipping_cents, do: 499", "path" => "solution.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-b6898ad39e4da810", "name" => "edit"}], "Let me analyze the code against the spec.\n\nSpec: `total(quantity, unit_cents, discount_pct \\\\ 0)`:\n- merchandise = quantity * unit_cents\n- discounted by discount_pct percent (integer 0..100 — anything else must raise)\n- plus a fixed 499-cent shipping fee\n- Shipping is excluded from the discount\n- Shipping is waived entirely when quantity is 0\n- Quantity and unit_cents are nonnegative integers; anything else must raise.\n\nCurrent code:\n```elixir\ndef total(quantity, unit_cents, discount_pct \\\\ 0) when quantity >= 0 do\n  gross = quantity * unit_cents\n  discounted = gross - div(gross * discount_pct, 100)\n  max(discounted - shipping_cents(), 0) + shipping_cents()\nend\n```\n\nBugs:\n1. The final line `max(discounted - shipping_cents(), 0) + shipping_cents()` is wrong. It should be `discounted + shipping_cents()` and shipping waived when quantity == 0.\n2. No validation of discount_pct (must be integer 0..100, else raise).\n3. No validation of unit_cents (must be nonnegative integer).\n4. Guard only `quantity >= 0`, doesn't check integer type, doesn't raise for non-integer/non-numeric. Actually `is_integer(quantity) and quantity >= 0` would be the guard.\n5. Shipping waived when quantity is 0 — currently shipping always added.\n\nLet me think about the minimal fix. The intended behavior:\n- total = discounted + shipping, where shipping = 0 if quantity == 0 else 499.\n\nThe `max(discounted - shipping_cents(), 0) + shipping_cents()` line is bizarre. Likely the bug was meant to be a correct computation. Let me rewrite minimally but correctly.\n\nI need to add validation that raises for invalid inputs. The spec says \"anything else must raise\". Functions in Elixir raise via FunctionClauseError if guards don't match.\n\nLet me design:\n\n```elixir\ndef total(quantity, unit_cents, discount_pct \\\\ 0)\n    when is_integer(quantity) and quantity >= 0\n    when is_integer(unit_cents) and unit_cents >= 0\n    when is_integer(discount_pct) and discount_pct >= 0 and discount_pct <= 100 do\n  gross = quantity * unit_cents\n  discounted = gross - div(gross * discount_pct, 100)\n  discounted + shipping_cents(quantity)\nend\n\ndefp shipping_cents(quantity) when quantity == 0, do: 0\ndefp shipping_cents(_quantity), do: 499\n```\n\nWait, but `shipping_cents/0` is the private helper. I can keep `shipping_cents` and add waiver logic. But changing the private function signature is fine (private). The requirement: keep public API (total/2, total/3) the same. Yes.\n\nBut careful: guards in multiple `when` clauses are joined with `and`. Good.\n\nHowever the original `defp shipping_cents, do: 499`. I could keep it and just inline the waiver. Minimal change: keep `defp shipping_cents, do: 499` and in total use `if quantity == 0, do: 0, else: shipping_cents()`. But changing the final buggy line is necessary.\n\nLet me keep `shipping_cents/0` unchanged and compute:\n\n```elixir\ndef total(quantity, unit_cents, discount_pct \\\\ 0)\n    when is_integer(quantity) and quantity >= 0\n    when is_integer(unit_cents) and unit_cents >= 0\n    when is_integer(discount_pct) and discount_pct >= 0 and discount_pct <= 100 do\n  gross = quantity * unit_cents\n  discounted = gross - div(gross * discount_pct, 100)\n  if quantity == 0 do\n    0\n  else\n    discounted + shipping_cents()\n  end\nend\n```\n\nWait when quantity == 0, gross = 0, discounted = 0, so 0 + shipping would be 499 but shipping waived so 0. So `if quantity == 0, do: 0, else: discounted + shipping_cents()` gives 0. Alternatively `discounted + (if quantity == 0, do: 0, else: shipping_cents())`.\n\nActually simpler: shipping = if quantity == 0, do: 0, else: shipping_cents(); total = discounted + shipping. When quantity==0, discounted is 0 anyway.\n\nLet me verify discount calculation: integer discount, div rounds toward zero (floor for nonneg). gross*discount_pct/100. That's standard. Spec doesn't specify rounding so div is fine.\n\nNow let me also double check guards: discount_pct default 0 passes. unit_cents guard. quantity guard.\n\nOne concern: Elixir `when` with multiple `when`s in a head are ANDed — correct.\n\nLet me write the fix.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 07:36:08.128716Z], "e8413600-f14f-4cc2-a81e-af51c6781b18"]
