INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{}, 9, :assistant, "f4ccd4bb-d017-48da-bdbb-1171cb21bc88", [%{"arguments" => %{"command" => "cd \"$(pwd)\" && cat > scratch/probe2.exs <<'EOF'\ndefmodule T do\n  def f(x, y) when is_integer(x) and x >= 0\n              when is_integer(y) and y >= 0 do\n    x + y\n  end\nend\ntry do IO.inspect(T.f(1, 10.5), label: \"multiwhen\") catch e -> IO.inspect(e, label: \"caught\") end\nEOF\nelixir scratch/probe2.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-bccdae9c6c9316f4", "name" => "bash"}], "So `Pricing.total(1, 10.5)` is reaching the body. So the multiple-`when` syntax is NOT ANDing all guards. Let me reconsider. In Elixir, multiple `when` in a head... Actually I now recall the rule: repeated `when` is allowed and treated as a list of guards, which are ANDed together. But here it's not. \n\nWait, maybe the issue is default arguments. Elixir docs: \"Multiple function clauses with default arguments must...\" Actually there might be a quirk where the guard is being applied incorrectly because of the `\\\\`.\n\nActually let me just test the multiple-when behavior independently.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 07:36:53.760549Z], "8900cfae-2cc4-4480-a458-6219e8ac7ac3"]
