INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{}, 3, :assistant, "e5f1b558-e34a-48d3-8e35-5d708809d394", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "    |> String.replace(~r/[^a-z0-9]+/, \"-\")\n    |> String.trim(\"-\")", "old_string" => "    |> String.replace(~r/[^a-z0-9]/, \"-\")", "path" => "solution.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-b296de1b2f9e70c6", "name" => "edit"}], "The bug: `String.replace(~r/[^a-z0-9]/, \"-\")` replaces each non-alphanumeric char individually, so runs produce multiple hyphens, and leading/trailing hyphens appear. Spec: any run of one or more non-alphanumeric chars is ONE separator, no leading/trailing hyphen, empty string stays empty.\n\nMinimal fix: use `~r/[^a-z0-9]+/` and trim leading/trailing hyphens. Note `\"  A--B  \"` => \"a-b\": with `+`, `\"  a--b  \"` becomes `-a-b-`... wait `--` is not alphanumeric either, so `[^a-z0-9]+` matches `--` too. `\"  a--b  \"` -> `-a-b-`. Then trim -> `a-b`. Good. Empty string `\"\"` -> `\"\"` (no match), trim gives `\"\"`. Good. `\"Elixir 1.19\"` -> `\"elixir-1-19\"`. Good. `\"Hello, World!\"` -> `\"hello-world-\"` -> trim -> `\"hello-world\"`. Good.\n\nMinimal change: add `+` to the regex and pipe through `String.trim(&1, \"-\")`.\n\nLet me verify with a quick test if elixir is available.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 07:48:16.860820Z], "5d15c4d8-2564-4806-8136-90c209b9b8b1"]
